  ('carex-maorica', 'Carex maorica', null, null, null, 'contested', false, false, false, 'C3', true, 'SP-015', 'C3: Separate stock lines, or one a local form of the other (nickname "oio")?', '{"commonName":"Māori sedge","maoriNames":[],"nameNote":"NZPCN recognises Carex maorica as a distinct species and does not list Carex secta as its synonym. WRT nursery identity remains unresolved; these species-specific references do not resolve which stock a historic record represented. Keep SP-015 and SP-016 separate. No verified Māori vernacular name was found; Māori sedge is the documented common name.","summary":"An endemic tufted sedge of freshwater wetlands, streambanks, lake margins and damp forest. Its long pale green leaves surround stems carrying several crowded flowering spikes.","lookFor":"Look for long folded leaves and several short female spikes clustered close to the base of a terminal male spike. Confirm flowering material before distinguishing similar sedges.","sources":[{"label":"New Zealand Plant Conservation Network","url":"https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora/species/carex-maorica/"}],"checkedOn":"2026-10-04","photoCheck":{"status":"partial","reason":"The botanical profile and three distinct licensed images of Carex maorica are confirmed. The separate WRT nursery-stock identity question involving Carex secta remains unresolved; no Carex secta image or identification has been substituted.","summary":"These illustrate Carex maorica. WRT must confirm which species its disputed nursery records represent.","checkedOn":"2026-10-04"}}'::jsonb, '[{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Carex_maorica_Hamlin_%28AM_AK294597%29.jpg/960px-Carex_maorica_Hamlin_%28AM_AK294597%29.jpg","width":960,"height":1280,"caption":"Carex maorica living tuft in habitat.","author":"Ewen Cameron / Auckland Museum","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carex_maorica_Hamlin_