  ('carmichaelia-crassicaulis', 'Carmichaelia crassicaulis', null, null, null, 'contested', false, true, false, 'C6', true, 'SP-022', 'C6: Is the racemosa variety its own line, and is Carmichaelia racemosa (potting Summary) the same as it? Also named on Plants Out Master > "plants removed from list"; status of that list is unexplained.', '{"commonName":"Coral broom","maoriNames":[],"nameNote":"Flora of New Zealand recognises subsp. crassicaulis and subsp. racemosa; this species-level entry does not assign either. Corallospartium crassicaule is an older synonym. WRT’s disputed identity remains unresolved, and subspecies threat assessments are not applied to its planting records.","summary":"An endemic broom with rigid branching stems and few visible leaves. Its yellowish branchlets are grooved, and small cream to pale pink pea flowers form clusters along them.","lookFor":"Stout grooved branchlets and tightly grouped pea flowers, often with purple markings. Small dry pods follow flowering; subspecies identification needs closer botanical examination.","sources":[{"label":"Flora of New Zealand","url":"https://www.nzflora.info/factsheet/taxon/Carmichaelia-crassicaulis.html"},{"label":"NZPCN · typical subspecies reference","url":"https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora/species/carmichaelia-crassicaulis-subsp-crassicaulis/"},{"label":"Otago Regional Council · species common name","url":"https://www.orc.govt.nz/environment/biosecurity-and-pests/plant-pests/gorse-and-broom"}],"checkedOn":"2026-10-04","photoCheck":{"status":"partial","reason":"Species-level identity confirmed; WRT subspecies or database-boundary ruling remains unresolved.","summary":"Species-level references are available. WRT must confirm its nursery identity before any subspecies is assigned.","checkedOn":"2026-10-04"}}'::jsonb, '[{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Carmichaelia_crassicaulis_463247951.jpg/960px-Carmichaelia_crassicaulis_463247951.jpg","width":960,"height":640,"caption":"Carmichaelia crassicaulis flowers in a species-labelled reference photographed by Joe Dillon; no subspecies is assigned to WRT’s record.","author":"Joe Dillon","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carmichaelia_crassicaulis_463247951.jpg","articleUrl":"https://www.nzflora.info/factsheet/taxon/Carmichaelia-crassicaulis.html","retrievedAt":"2026-10-04","focalPoint":"50% 50%","sourceName":"Wikimedia Commons","articleLabel":"Flora of New Zealand species reference"},{"src":"https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/463247939/large.jpeg","width":1024,"height":683,"caption":"Carmichaelia crassicaulis branching habit. Research-grade iNaturalist reference; no subspecies assigned to WRT records.","author":"Joe Dillon","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","sourceUrl":"https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/463247939","articleUrl":"https://www.nzflora.info/factsheet/taxon/Carmichaelia-crassicaulis.html","retrievedAt":"2026-10-04","focalPoint":"50% 50%","sourceName":"iNaturalist","articleLabel":"Flora of New Zealand species reference","observationUrl":"https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/258212600"},{"src":"https://inaturalist-open-data.s3.amazonaws.com/photos/463247945/large.jpeg","width":1024,"height":683,"caption":"Carmichaelia crassicaulis flower detail. Research-grade iNaturalist reference; no subspecies assigned to WRT records.","author":"Joe Dillon","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","sourceUrl":"https://www.inaturalist.org/photos/463247945","articleUrl":"https://www.nzflora.info/factsheet/taxon/Carmichaelia-crassicaulis.html","retrievedAt":"2026-10-04","focalPoint":"50% 50%","sourceName":"iNaturalist","articleLabel":"Flora of New Zealand species reference","observationUrl":"https://www.inaturalist.org/observations/258212600"}]'::jsonb),
