  ('muehlenbeckia-complexa', 'Muehlenbeckia complexa', null, 'Wire vine', 'Pōhuehue', 'core', false, false, false, null, false, 'SP-103', null, '{"commonName":"Wire vine","maoriNames":["Pōhuehue","Pōhue","Pōpōhue","Tororaro","Waekāhu"],"nameNote":"Flora of New Zealand records these vernacular names. Pōhuehue is shared with other climbers, including Muehlenbeckia australis; Tororaro is also used for other Muehlenbeckia species. NZPCN recognises varieties; this species-level profile does not assign a variety to WRT’s records.","summary":"A native climbing or sprawling plant with many interlacing stems. It grows over other vegetation and can form dense tangled masses.","lookFor":"Small rounded or broadly oval leaves on wiry stems. Tiny pale flowers occur along the shoots, followed by dark seeds surrounded by pale fleshy flower parts.","sources":[{"label":"Flora of New Zealand","url":"https://www.nzflora.info/factsheet/Taxon/Muehlenbeckia-complexa.html"},{"label":"NZPCN · names for the typical variety","url":"https://www.nzpcn.org.nz/flora/species/muehlenbeckia-complexa-var-complexa/"},{"label":"Wikipedia · shared name","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muehlenbeckia_complexa"}],"checkedOn":"2026-10-04","photoCheck":{"status":"confirmed","reason":"Identity and profile checked; three licensed source images actually viewed.","checkedOn":"2026-10-04"}}'::jsonb, '[{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Muehlenbeckia_complexawith_flowers.jpeg","width":945,"height":2048,"caption":"Muehlenbeckia complexa foliage and small pale flowers at Waikanae Beach, New Zealand.","author":"Stuart Yeates","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muehlenbeckia_complexawith_flowers.jpeg","articleUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muehlenbeckia_complexa","retrievedAt":"2026-10-04","focalPoint":"50% 50%","sourceName":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org